// To define a diagnostic, follow the Template format below and add the same name to the DiagnosticCode enum. Every entry states its Category (SPEC 23.3.6.1); Severity defaults to Error. A message takes at most two arguments ({0}, {1}) and no free text; Arguments names each as name:Kind (Number, Enumeration, Boolean, Text or Type), and they become the Reason. Evidence names further facts a report may add to the Reason, all of them or none. A Label may reference the Reason's facts in order, arguments then evidence.

  + Name="Template_Kd"
    Severity="Error"
    Category="Language"
    Message="The primary diagnostic message"
    Label="A short label describing the relevant code"
    Advice="Conditional repair advice; no edit is inferred from it"
    Note="Additional information about the diagnostic"

